{
  "slug": "maister",
  "name": "Maister",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Structured, standards-aware SDLC orchestration for Claude Code — 5 workflow types, 23 agents, 15+ skills, visual companion server for product design.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **17 skills**, **25 agents**, **6 commands**, **2 hooks** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (17): `codebase-analyzer` (Analyzes codebase using adaptive parallel Explore subagents based on task complexity), `development` (Unified orchestrator for all development tasks), `docs-manager` (Internal engine for managing project documentation and technical standards in .maister/docs/), `implementation-plan-executor` (Execute implementation plans by delegating each task group to task-group-implementer subagent), `implementation-verifier` (Verify completed implementations for quality assurance), `init` (Initialize Maister framework with intelligent project analysis and documentation generation), `migration` (Orchestrates the complete migration workflow from current state analysis through implementation to compatibility verification), `mockup-studio` (Generates UI mockups (rendered HTML/CSS via a browser visual companion, or terminal ASCII)), and 9 more\n- **Agents** (25): `ascii-mockup-generator` (Generates ASCII mockups showing UI layout and integration with existing components), `bottleneck-analyzer` (Static code analysis agent identifying performance bottlenecks by reading source code, schema files, and query patterns), `code-quality-pragmatist` (Pragmatic code review specialist detecting over-engineering, unnecessary complexity, and developer experience issues), `code-reviewer` (Automated code quality, security, and performance analysis), `codebase-analysis-reporter` (Merges raw findings from parallel Explore agents into a structured codebase analysis report), `docs-operator` (Internal documentation management service), `e2e-test-verifier` (Executes runtime browser verification using Playwright MCP tools to verify implementation behavior against specifications), `gap-analyzer` (Compares current vs desired state, identifies gaps with user journey and data lifecycle analysis), and 17 more\n- **Commands** (6): `reviews-code` (Run automated code quality, security, and performance analysis on your code), `reviews-pragmatic` (Run pragmatic code review to detect over-engineering and ensure code matches project scale), `reviews-production-readiness` (Verify production deployment readiness with comprehensive checks), `reviews-reality-check` (Comprehensive reality assessment of completed work to verify it actually works and is production-ready), `reviews-spec-audit` (Independent specification audit to verify completeness and clarity before implementation), `work` (Unified entry point — auto-classifies tasks and routes to appropriate workflow)\n- **Hooks** (2): `SessionStart`, `PreToolUse`\n- **MCP servers** (1): `playwright`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install maister@claude-community` from `SkillPanel/maister` (`plugins/maister`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
